{#
  THE INVITATION.

  ── THE DIRECTION, IN ONE SENTENCE ──────────────────────────────────────────
  An engraved ceremony invitation: deep ink ground, a single gold rule, a serif
  display face over monospace metadata, letterpress restraint. No gradients, no
  glass, no pill badges, no icon rows.

  ── WHY IT IS NOT THE CAMPAIGN SKELETON ─────────────────────────────────────
  The first version of this rendered through emails/campaign.twig's block list, which
  was the wrong call and looked it: that skeleton is built for a broadcast — a
  countdown hero, numbered asks, a green CTA — and an invitation to be honoured in
  public is not a broadcast. It is addressed to one person, it has one thing to say,
  and the design has to carry that or the words are wasted.

  What it DOES inherit from that skeleton is the scaffolding, deliberately: the
  fluid-hybrid 560px wrapper, the MSO conditional tables, the VML button, the styled
  alt text, presentation roles on every layout table, the hidden preheader, no data:
  URIs. Those twelve properties are held by EmailInboxCompatTest and they are the
  difference between a design and a design that arrives.

  ── THE HIERARCHY, AND WHAT LEFT IT ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Two actions survive on the surface: open your pass, and get your guests' tickets.
  Everything else an invitee might want — the schedule, the venue map, the programme
  — is one tap away on the event page and is NOT here. An invitation with six links
  is a newsletter.

  Type: Georgia for the display voice (present on every mail client that matters and
  with real character — a web font cannot be relied on here); Helvetica/Arial for
  body; Consolas/Courier for the micro-labels and the reference, because a reference
  is read aloud at a door and monospace is what makes it transcribable.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
{# iOS turns dates, addresses and references into blue links and then restyles them.
   A ceremony date rendered as a system link in the middle of an engraved invitation
   is the single ugliest thing this template can do, so it is switched off. #}
<meta name="format-detection" content="telephone=no, date=no, address=no, email=no, url=no">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
<title>{{ subject }}</title>
<!--[if mso]>
<xml><o:OfficeDocumentSettings><o:PixelsPerInch>96</o:PixelsPerInch></o:OfficeDocumentSettings></xml>
<style>
  /* Word engine: no rem, and cells need mso-line-height-rule or the leading is ignored.
     Deliberately no angle-bracketed tag names in this comment — the balance check counts
     tags inside an [if mso] block, and a tag named in prose here reads as an unclosed one. */
  table, td, div, p, a { font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif !important; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; }
</style>
<![endif]-->
<style>
  /* Gmail strips this block in several configurations — POP/IMAP accounts most
     commonly — so nothing below is load-bearing. It refines; it does not lay out. */
  .ag-w { width:100% !important; max-width:560px !important; }
  .ag-px { padding-left:32px !important; padding-right:32px !important; }
  a { color:#8a6205; }
  /* iOS still detects dates and addresses with format-detection set, wraps them in its
     own anchor and restyles them blue. A ceremony date rendered as a system link in the
     middle of an engraved invitation is the ugliest thing this template could do. */
  a[x-apple-data-detectors] {
    color:inherit !important; text-decoration:none !important; font-size:inherit !important;
    font-family:inherit !important; font-weight:inherit !important; line-height:inherit !important;
  }
  @media only screen and (max-width:600px) {
    .ag-px  { padding-left:22px !important; padding-right:22px !important; }
    .ag-d1  { font-size:29px !important; line-height:34px !important; }
    .ag-name{ font-size:21px !important; line-height:27px !important; }
    .ag-fact{ display:block !important; width:100% !important; padding-bottom:14px !important; }
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    /* Apple Mail and iOS honour this and leave the rest alone; Gmail and Outlook.com
       invert regardless and do it badly on near-white, which is why the card is a
       warm off-white rather than #ffffff — an inverted #ffffff goes flat black and
       takes the gold with it. */
    .ag-body { background-color:#0b1f22 !important; }
    .ag-card { background-color:#12292c !important; }
    .ag-ink  { color:#f2f4f3 !important; }
    .ag-mute { color:#a8bbba !important; }
    .ag-rule { border-color:#2a4a4c !important; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body class="ag-body" style="margin:0; padding:0; background-color:#e9ecec; -webkit-text-size-adjust:100%; -ms-text-size-adjust:100%;">

{# The preheader: the line an inbox shows beside the subject. Hidden, and padded with
   zero-width joiners so the client does not pull body copy in after it. #}
<div style="display:none; max-height:0; max-width:0; font-size:1px; line-height:1px; opacity:0; overflow:hidden; mso-hide:all;">
  {{ preheader }}&#8202;&zwnj;&#8202;&zwnj;&#8202;&zwnj;&#8202;&zwnj;&#8202;&zwnj;&#8202;&zwnj;&#8202;&zwnj;
</div>

<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#e9ecec" class="ag-body" style="background-color:#e9ecec;">
  <tr>
    <td align="center" style="padding:28px 12px 40px 12px;">

      <!--[if mso]>
      <table role="presentation" width="560" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:560px;"><tr><td>
      <![endif]-->
      <table role="presentation" class="agw-wrapper ag-w ag-card" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:100%; max-width:560px; background-color:#fdfdfc; border:1px solid #d7dcdb;">

        {# ── 1 · THE MASTHEAD BAND ─────────────────────────────────────────
           Ink, the wordmark in tracked monospace gold, and one gold rule under it.
           That rule is the only ornament in the whole email and it is doing the work
           an engraved border does on a printed card. #}
        <tr>
          <td bgcolor="#10292c" style="background-color:#10292c; padding:22px 32px 20px 32px;" class="ag-px">
            <p style="margin:0; font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace; font-size:12px; letter-spacing:3.4px; color:#f3b416; text-transform:uppercase;">Africa&nbsp;GATES</p>
            <p style="margin:5px 0 0 0; font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:12px; font-style:italic; color:#9fb3b2;">An Afrovanguard Initiative</p>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr><td bgcolor="#f3b416" style="background-color:#f3b416; height:3px; line-height:3px; font-size:0;">&nbsp;</td></tr>

        {# ── 2 · THE STATEMENT ─────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        <tr>
          <td class="ag-px" style="padding:38px 32px 0 32px;">
            <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:2.2px; color:#8a6205; text-transform:uppercase;">Invitation &middot; {{ audience_one }}</p>
            <h1 class="ag-d1 ag-ink" style="margin:0; font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:35px; line-height:40px; font-weight:normal; color:#10292c; letter-spacing:-0.4px;">You are invited</h1>
            <p class="ag-mute" style="margin:14px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15.5px; line-height:25px; color:#4a5c5e;">
              to <strong style="color:#10292c;">{{ event_title }}</strong>, as a guest of honour.
            </p>
          </td>
        </tr>

        {# ── 3 · THE NAME PLATE ────────────────────────────────────────────
           The engraved bit. Their name, set between two hairlines, in the display
           face — because this is addressed to one person and the design should be
           unable to pretend otherwise. #}
        <tr>
          <td class="ag-px" style="padding:30px 32px 0 32px;">
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
              <tr><td class="ag-rule" style="border-top:1px solid #ddd; font-size:0; line-height:0;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
              <tr>
                <td align="center" style="padding:20px 6px 20px 6px;">
                  <p class="ag-name ag-ink" style="margin:0; font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:25px; line-height:32px; font-style:italic; color:#10292c;">{{ name }}</p>
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr><td class="ag-rule" style="border-top:1px solid #ddd; font-size:0; line-height:0;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
            </table>
          </td>
        </tr>

        {# ── 4 · THE REASON ────────────────────────────────────────────────
           One sentence, operator-written per programme. It is the only italic body
           copy in the email, which is what makes it read as the sentence that matters. #}
        <tr>
          <td class="ag-px" style="padding:26px 32px 0 32px;">
            <p class="ag-ink" style="margin:0; font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:17px; line-height:29px; color:#1e3b3e;">
              We want the hall packed {{ witness }} — and we would like the people who know that work best to be in the room to see it recognised.
            </p>
          </td>
        </tr>

        {% if cover_url %}
        {# ── 5 · THE EVENING, PICTURED ─────────────────────────────────────
           width AND height on the tag, always: a blocked remote image with no height
           collapses the panel it is the hero of, and Outlook desktop blocks by
           default. The alt text is styled for the same reason — unstyled alt renders
           as 10px serif and reads as a broken attachment rather than a sentence. #}
        <tr>
          <td style="padding:30px 0 0 0;">
            <img src="{{ cover_url }}" width="560" height="220" alt="{{ event_title }}"
                 style="display:block; width:100%; max-width:560px; height:auto; border:0; outline:none; text-decoration:none; font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:14px; line-height:22px; color:#4a5c5e; background-color:#e9ecec;">
          </td>
        </tr>
        {% endif %}

        {# ── 6 · THE FACTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
           Two cells, monospace micro-labels above each. Stacks on a phone via the
           .ag-fact media rule — and if Gmail strips the <style>, it stays a
           two-column table, which is legible rather than broken. #}
        <tr>
          <td class="ag-px" style="padding:32px 32px 0 32px;">
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
              <tr>
                <td class="ag-fact" width="50%" valign="top" style="padding:0 12px 0 0;">
                  <p style="margin:0 0 6px 0; font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace; font-size:10px; letter-spacing:1.6px; color:#8a6205; text-transform:uppercase;">When</p>
                  <p class="ag-ink" style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:23px; color:#10292c;">{{ when }}</p>
                </td>
                <td class="ag-fact" width="50%" valign="top" style="padding:0 0 0 12px;">
                  <p style="margin:0 0 6px 0; font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace; font-size:10px; letter-spacing:1.6px; color:#8a6205; text-transform:uppercase;">Where</p>
                  <p class="ag-ink" style="margin:0; font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:23px; color:#10292c;">{{ where ?: 'Venue to be confirmed' }}</p>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
          </td>
        </tr>

        {# ── 7 · THE PASS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
           An ink panel, because it is the one thing in the email that is a
           credential rather than a message. Gold VML button for Outlook, real anchor
           for everything else. #}
        <tr>
          <td class="ag-px" style="padding:32px 32px 0 32px;">
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#10292c" style="background-color:#10292c;">
              <tr>
                <td align="center" style="padding:26px 24px 26px 24px;">
                  <p style="margin:0 0 6px 0; font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace; font-size:10px; letter-spacing:1.8px; color:#f3b416; text-transform:uppercase;">Your entry</p>
                  <p style="margin:0 0 18px 0; font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14.5px; line-height:23px; color:#dfe7e6;">
                    Arranged already — no ticket needed for you. Your pass is a live page: open it on your phone at the door.
                  </p>

                  <!--[if mso]>
                  <v:roundrect xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" href="{{ id_url }}" style="height:46px; v-text-anchor:middle; width:220px;" arcsize="9%" strokecolor="#f3b416" fillcolor="#f3b416">
                    <w:anchorlock/>
                    <center style="color:#1a1204; font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; font-weight:bold;">Open your pass</center>
                  </v:roundrect>
                  <![endif]-->
                  <!--[if !mso]><!-->
                  <a href="{{ id_url }}" style="display:inline-block; background-color:#f3b416; color:#1a1204; font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; font-weight:bold; line-height:46px; text-align:center; text-decoration:none; width:220px; border-radius:4px;">Open your pass</a>
                  <!--<![endif]-->
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
          </td>
        </tr>

        {# ── 8 · THE ASK ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
           Their reference, in monospace, framed. It is both their identity at the
           door and the code their guests spend, which is why it is set apart rather
           than mentioned in a sentence. #}
        <tr>
          <td class="ag-px" style="padding:32px 32px 0 32px;">
            <p style="margin:0 0 14px 0; font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:2.2px; color:#8a6205; text-transform:uppercase;">Bring your people</p>
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="border:1px solid #f3b416;">
              <tr>
                <td align="center" style="padding:18px 18px 16px 18px;">
                  <p class="ag-ink" style="margin:0; font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace; font-size:19px; letter-spacing:2.4px; color:#10292c;">{{ reference }}</p>
                  <p class="ag-mute" style="margin:8px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12.5px; line-height:19px; color:#5a6d6f;">
                    {{ discount }}% off &middot; up to {{ quota }} guests
                  </p>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="ag-mute" style="margin:14px 0 0 0; font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14.5px; line-height:24px; color:#4a5c5e;">
              Share it with the people you want in the room. It takes {{ discount }}% off their tickets, for up to {{ quota }} of them{% if tier_line %}{{ tier_line }}{% endif %}.
              <a href="{{ events_url }}" style="color:#8a6205; text-decoration:underline;">Send them to the tickets &rarr;</a>
            </p>
          </td>
        </tr>

        {# ── 9 · SIGN-OFF ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
        <tr>
          <td class="ag-px" style="padding:34px 32px 0 32px;">
            <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
              <tr><td class="ag-rule" style="border-top:1px solid #ddd; font-size:0; line-height:0;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
            </table>
            <p class="ag-ink" style="margin:22px 0 0 0; font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:16px; line-height:27px; color:#1e3b3e;">
              We would be honoured to have you with us. The formal invitation is attached, for your records.
            </p>
            <p class="ag-ink" style="margin:18px 0 0 0; font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:16px; line-height:24px; color:#10292c;">
              With respect,<br>
              <strong style="font-weight:normal;">Africa GATES</strong>
            </p>
          </td>
        </tr>

        <tr><td style="padding:0 0 38px 0; font-size:0; line-height:0;">&nbsp;</td></tr>
      </table>

      {# ── FOOTER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
         Outside the card, in monospace, small and quiet. An invitation that ends in
         a marketing footer stops being an invitation. #}
      <table role="presentation" class="ag-w" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:100%; max-width:560px;">
        <tr>
          <td align="center" style="padding:20px 24px 0 24px;">
            <p style="margin:0; font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace; font-size:11px; line-height:19px; color:#7a8b8c;">
              {{ postal_address }}<br>
              <a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}" style="color:#7a8b8c; text-decoration:underline;">Stop receiving email from Africa GATES</a>
            </p>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <!--[if mso]></td></tr></table><![endif]-->

    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
